WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
Antarctica's ice sheet covers
almost 14 million square kilometres.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.970
Greenland's covers about 1.7 million.

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.110
They are the only two ice sheets on Earth.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.750
Smaller glaciers grow in Alaska,
in Patagonia and in the Himalaya.

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.510
And frozen ground lies under about 25 per
cent of the Northern Hemisphere's exposed

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.810
land.

7
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.090
Ice in some places,
frozen ground in others.

8
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.270
So what decides where cold places lie?

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.110
In this mission, you'll
sort polar, alpine,

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.810
glacial and periglacial environments,
and see how their climate,

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.250
soils and plants interact.

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.950
Then you'll read a climate
graph for Utqiaġvik,

13
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.750
Alaska, where monthly means stay below
freezing for 8 months of the year.

14
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.010
Your mission: find out what controls
where cold environments occur.
